# CMPG111 – Introduction to Computing & Programming

## 📘 Module Overview
CMPG111 introduces foundational programming concepts essential for all computing modules.  
This enhanced repository version aligns with NWU’s academic outcomes while presenting content suitable for GitHub portfolios.

## 🎯 Learning Outcomes
Students completing this module will be able to:
- Understand variables, operators, and data types
- Write programs using conditionals and loops
- Use functions to structure modular code
- Apply algorithmic thinking to solve computing problems
- Debug and test simple programs
- Develop foundational computational problem‑solving skills

## 🧩 Topics Covered
### 1. Introduction to Programming
- What is a program?
- Problem-solving & algorithms  
- Pseudocode & flowcharts

### 2. Variables & Data Types
- Integers, floats, strings, booleans  
- Basic operations  
- Input & output

### 3. Control Flow
- If, elif, else  
- Logical operators  
- Nested decisions

### 4. Repetition Structures
- For loops  
- While loops  
- Loop control (break, continue)

### 5. Functions
- Parameters & return types  
- Scope  
- Modular design

### 6. Basic Algorithms
- Searching  
- Sorting  
- Mathematical algorithms

### 7. Debugging Techniques
- Common errors  
- Trace tables  
- Print debugging

## 🛠 Tools & Technologies
- Python (primary example language)
- VS Code / PyCharm
- Git & GitHub

## 🚀 Skills You Will Gain
- Structured programming
- Algorithmic thinking
- Clean coding habits
- Problem-solving fundamentals
- Familiarity with Git version control

